    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it takes time but it feels weirdly inconsistent. like, some parts of the web see the change but others just stay stuck on the old one for no reason. is there anything specifically causing the bits that don't update? like what's actually happening behind the scenes to keep the old info cached?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That inconsistency you're seeing is because different parts of the internet are caching the old information at different rates. Each recursive DNS resolver—the servers your users query—has its own local cache, and they honor the Time-To-Live (TTL) value set on your old records. If the TTL was set high, those local caches are stubborn, holding onto the old IP address until their designated expiry time. You can't force every single server to update instantly; it's a matter of waiting for those individual caches to expire.",
      "source": "target",
